## Project Description
This sub-project demonstrates how to deploy and manage a static web server inside a lightweight Docker container using **Nginx (Alpine)**. It covers Docker containerization basics, container lifecycle management, and best practices.

---

## 1. Container Lifecycle & Essential Commands
To understand the lifecycle of a container, the following commands are used to build, run, and manage this web server:

### A. Build Phase (Creating the Image)
To build the custom Nginx image using the Dockerfile:
```bash
docker build -t my-web-server:v1 .
B. Run Phase (Deployment)
To run the container in the background (detached mode) and forward port 8080 to container's port 80
docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name running-web-server my-web-server:v1
:Inspect Logs: To check web server access logs and errors:
  docker logs running-web-server
  Resource Stats: To monitor CPU, Memory, and Network usage in real-time:
    docker stats running-web-server
    Container Inspection: To view low-level configuration details (like IP address):
    
      docker inspect running-web-server
      
